@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix cco:  <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/> .
@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> .

<https://example.org/ontology-tradecraft/qudt-mapping> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:comment "QUDT -> CCOM/CCO mappings from review of ccom-qudt-structural-matches.xlsx (645 candidate pairs: 43 CCO classes x 15 QUDT unit classes)." .

### Kept rows: each QUDT unit class <-> CCO Information Content Entity (cco:ont00000958).
### A measurement unit is a conventional standard that measurement values refer to. It does not inhere
### in any one bearer and can be copied across documents and systems, which is what CCO means by
### information content. The three top-level unit classes in the file are mapped; the other 12
### (Physical, Space And Time, Mechanics, Currency, ...) are subclasses of these in QUDT and inherit it.
qudt:ScienceAndEngineeringUnit rdfs:subClassOf cco:ont00000958 .   # Information Content Entity
qudt:FinancialUnit             rdfs:subClassOf cco:ont00000958 .
qudt:HumanUnit                 rdfs:subClassOf cco:ont00000958 .
